course: dictionary
lesson: 9649
title: Subdue: control, calm and quiet
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To subdue something is to bring it under control, or to make it calmer or quieter. You can subdue people, feelings or sounds. «The army subdued the rebels» means the army got control over them, usually by force.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. In «She tried to subdue her nerves before the test», her nerves are feelings, so subdue means calm them down, not beat them. Try your meaning in the sentence: "She tried to calm her nerves" still makes sense, so you have got it.
explain: Light and sound can be subdued too. A subdued light is softer and dimmer, and a subdued laugh is held back and quieter. Ask yourself what is being subdued, and that tells you which meaning fits.
fact: Subdue means to get control over a person, group or country, usually by force.
fact: «The Romans subdued much of Britain» means they took control of much of it.
fact: To subdue a feeling means to calm it or hold it back, like «subduing your excitement».
fact: «Subdue a fire» means to bring it under control.
fact: To subdue light, colour or sound means to make it softer or quieter.
exercise: «The army subdued the rebels.» What does subdue mean here? | Sang them to sleep | Made them laugh | *Got control of them, usually by force | Gave them a present
exercise: «She tried to subdue her nerves before the test.» What is she trying to do to her nerves? | Make them louder | Forget about the test | *Calm them down | Grow them longer
exercise: Which of these describes a light that has been made softer and dimmer? | *A subdued light | A blazing light | A flashing light | A bright, sudden light
test: «Mum asked us to subdue our giggles in the library.» What should the children do? | Shout louder | Tell a joke | *Hold their giggles back and keep quiet | Leave the library
test: «The firefighters worked hard to subdue the blaze.» What does subdue mean here? | Paint it | Dance around it | *Bring it under control | Make it bigger
exam: «The hero managed to subdue the thief and hold him until the police came.» What does subdue mean in this sentence? | Thank | Forgive | *Overpower and bring under control | Race past
